evalharness is stdlib-only Python. It bundles no third-party code and no
third-party data. The items below are things it can *interoperate with* when
you supply them yourself. Each is licensed separately by its own owner, and
none of them are redistributed in this repository.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SiliconCrew — optional adapter, not vendored, not bundled
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Copyright (c) 2026 Naman Ranka
    License: MIT
    Repository: https://github.com/naman-ranka/siliconcrew
    Application: https://siliconcrew-frontend-psp2dkllmq-uc.a.run.app/

No SiliconCrew source code is included in or vendored into this repository.

evalharness includes an OPTIONAL read-only adapter (`evalctl import-baseline`,
MCP tool `import_baseline`) that can parse an already-graded CVDP results file
produced by SiliconCrew's bench-orchestrator, at:

    bench-orchestrator/final_runs/FINAL_MANIFEST.json

Those verdicts are imported as an EXTERNAL reference baseline. They were
produced by SiliconCrew's harness (its agent, model, and tools), not yours.
evalharness stamps them with a fixed synthetic harness id so they can never be
averaged into a measurement of your own system. Using this adapter is entirely
optional; evalharness works standalone without it. You must obtain the
manifest yourself from your own SiliconCrew run.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. NVIDIA CVDP benchmark dataset — NOT redistributed
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Copyright and license: NVIDIA Corporation, licensed separately by NVIDIA.

No CVDP dataset files, problems, prompts, contexts, patches, or harnesses are
included in this repository.

`evalctl import-cvdp` reads a CVDP dataset JSONL that YOU supply via
`--dataset` (or the CVDP_DATASET environment variable). You are responsible
for obtaining the dataset from NVIDIA and for complying with its license and
terms of use. evalharness only reads the file from your local disk; it never
downloads it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. ghcr.io/hdl/sim/osvb container image — NOT bundled
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
    Licensed separately by its own maintainers.

This container image is the reference simulation environment used for faithful
CVDP grading. It is not bundled, vendored, or pulled by evalharness. It is
mentioned only in documentation, and is needed only if you choose to run the
optional expensive path of grading CVDP problems in the official reference
container. Nothing in evalharness's core functionality requires Docker or this
image.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Network posture
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
evalharness core functionality makes zero network calls. It contains no
telemetry, no analytics, and no update checks. All state lives in a local
`.evalharness/` directory inside the repository you point it at. Nothing about
your source code, prompts, or results leaves your machine unless you choose to
send it.
